data/checkpoint_real_llm_*.jsonl

# v2.1 confirmatory campaign runtime state: per-arm checkpoints and
# operator wrapper scripts -- some of these (auto_resume.sh) embed a
# live API key inline for a background retry loop; none of this is
# source, all of it is regenerated (or superseded by the merged
# observations file) by re-running the campaign, and none of it should
# ever reach a commit. Globbed (runs*/, not just runs/) so a revision's
# own output dir (runs_v2/, and any future runs_v3/, ...) is covered
# automatically -- found on 2026-08-20 that runs_v2/ was NOT covered by
# the old literal pattern, leaving its auto_resume.sh (a live API key
# inline) one `git add -A` away from being committed.
#
# The two explicit exceptions below are the actual confirmatory
# evidence, not runtime scaffolding: receipts_2.jsonl (the state-machine
# log proving RUN_COMPLETED) and the merged, content-hashed raw
# observations file (21,478 rows, no secrets -- checked with a grep for
# key-shaped strings before un-ignoring, docs/audit.md defect #18).
# `**` (not a bare trailing `/`) so git still descends into runs*/ to
# evaluate these negations -- a directory-terminated pattern would
# ignore the whole tree before per-file rules are ever considered.
#
# The observations exception names the exact content hash, not a
# `confirmatory_observations_v21_*.jsonl` wildcard: a wildcard would
# also un-ignore data/protocol_v2_1/runs/'s own observations file, from
# an earlier interrupted attempt with a different hash -- superseded,
# not evidence, and never meant to leave this machine.
data/protocol_v2_1/runs*/**
!data/protocol_v2_1/runs_v2/receipts_2.jsonl
!data/protocol_v2_1/runs_v2/confirmatory_observations_v21_2d36433e861121928cceac5899ff1cf4ed346fe63250ff87956f8aba4f082c5c.jsonl

